From caeb568fdd16e163fb20d34120b24eedafc77835 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wray-lee <wray-lee@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:31:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(channels): bound channel network I/O and make poller
 supervision non-blocking

Every credentialed and download call on the poller path now carries a timeout
bound (telegram getUpdates/send, max, matrix sync/health, weixin getupdates
long-poll headroom), so a stalled socket returns a bounded error instead of
hanging the loop. Poller liveness is tracked separately from worker-turn
progress; a wedged or dispatching poller is detached or stopped past a hard
deadline instead of blocking supervisor shutdown, and a turn that progresses
without ever finishing is recovered.
